all_locations.csv
# location_data/ is NOT ignored any more. The three open-government inventories the paper
# actually ran on (bend.geojson, portland.geojson, nyc.csv -- 71.8 MB) were excluded here,
# which is why v1.0-iccv2025 shipped without the one input nobody else can reconstruct: the
# live portals serve current, drifting versions, so a later download is a *different* file.
# They are committed, hash-pinned in docs/data_provenance.md section 3, and marked binary in
# .gitattributes so no line-ending normalisation can alter those hashes.
# street_data/: the raw downloads stay ignored -- 801.6 MB, and "New York - Streets.geojson"
# alone is 669 MB, over GitHub's 100 MB hard limit. The *derivative* is committed instead.
# generate_negative_panos.py reads only the geometry plus one name field from these, so
# scripts/build_street_derivative.py strips the rest: 801.6 MB -> 18.7 MB, a 42.9x cut, with
# `verify` proving the sampled street network is bit-for-bit the same. The full downloads
# still take precedence if present, and go to Hugging Face (issue #21).
street_data/*
!street_data/*.min.geojson.gz
dataset.jsonl
finaldataset.jsonl
negativepanos.jsonl
negativepanosSHORTENED.jsonl
progress.txt
